+! Build 34: the free-free Gaunt factor of GFF_VEC (subs/gff.f) and its temperature derivative. Same table, the
+! same statements for U, GB, the cell (IU, IGB) and the weights (DU, DGB), so G equals GFF_VEC to the bit (checked
+! at run time). Inside the cell G is bilinear in (DU, DGB), and U = log10(4.7994 nu) - log10 T,
+! GB = log10(15.789 Z^2) - log10 T, DU = 2U + 9 - IU, DGB = 2GB + 7 - IGB, so
+!   dG/dlog10T = -2 dG/dDU [U not clamped] - 2 dG/dDGB [GB not clamped],  dG/dT = dG/dlog10T / (T ln 10).
+! A clamped argument (U outside (-3.99999999, 1.499999), GB outside (-2.99999999, 1.999999)) does not vary with T.
+! On a cell boundary (2U+9 or 2GB+7 an integer) G is continuous but not differentiable; the slope of the cell
+! GFF_VEC selects there (the one at larger U, GB) is returned.
+subroutine qs_gff_dt_vec(g,dgdt,rnu,t,zion,nd)
